# Assistant connection to ordin
error-block-plan-invalid = The plan needs between 3 and 7 steps, each 1 to 80 characters long. Adjust it and try again.
error-block-plan-position-invalid = That step isn't in the plan. Choose a step that is on the list.
error-block-plan-too-many-versions = This plan has been changed too many times. Start a new plan instead.
error-block-report-refused = The report couldn't be shown because its contents were not valid. Try again.
error-mcp-already-started = The assistant connection has already been started.
error-mcp-arguments-invalid = The details sent with that action weren't valid. Check them and try again.
error-mcp-arguments-too-large = The details sent with that action are too large. Send less and try again.
error-mcp-awaiting-approval = Still waiting for your approval. Approve or decline it when you're ready.
error-mcp-block-store-already-bound = Shown items are already being kept for this work.
error-mcp-block-store-not-bound = This report is too large to show, because nowhere is set up to keep it. Try a shorter report.
error-mcp-bridge-malformed = The assistant's connection to ordin didn't start properly. Try again.
error-mcp-bridge-peer-refused = Another user on this computer tried to connect to ordin, so the connection was refused.
error-mcp-bridge-protocol-unsupported = The assistant uses a version of the connection that this ordin can't talk to. Update ordin or Claude Code.
error-mcp-bridge-unauthenticated = The assistant couldn't prove it was started by ordin, so the connection was refused. Try again.
error-mcp-call-cancelled = That step was cancelled before it finished.
error-mcp-call-timeout = That step took too long and was stopped. Try again.
error-mcp-decision-failed = ordin couldn't get your approval for that step. Try again.
error-mcp-denied = Your rules don't allow that step, so it wasn't done.
error-mcp-invalid-name = That name can only use lower-case letters, digits and underscores, start with a letter, and be 32 characters or fewer.
error-mcp-journal-failed = The report couldn't be saved to your history. Try again.
error-mcp-not-started = The assistant connection isn't running yet. Try again in a moment.
error-mcp-output-truncated = The result was too long, so only the first part is shown.
error-mcp-plan-not-stated = A step can't be marked until a plan has been written. Write the plan first.
error-mcp-plan-one-now = Only one step can be marked as current at a time.
error-mcp-provider-duplicate = That source of actions has already been added.
error-mcp-provider-failed = A source of actions didn't answer in time, so its actions may be missing. Try again in a moment.
error-mcp-provider-panicked = A source of actions stopped working part-way through. Try again.
error-mcp-ref-resolver-already-bound = Links to shown items are already set up for this work.
error-mcp-ref-resolver-not-bound = ordin isn't ready to show reports and plans yet. Try again in a moment.
error-mcp-registry-frozen = Sources of actions can't be added once ordin has started.
error-mcp-rejected = The approval ran out of time with no answer, so the step wasn't done. Try again.
error-mcp-rest-offset-invalid = There's nothing left to read from that point in the result.
error-mcp-rest-unknown = The rest of that result is no longer available. Run the step again.
error-mcp-server-claimed = That name is already used by another source of actions, or is too similar to one. Choose a different name.
error-mcp-server-not-offered = That connection isn't available for this work.
error-mcp-session-closed = That step was cancelled because the work it belonged to had ended.
error-mcp-session-exists = This work already has an open connection.
error-mcp-session-unknown = ordin doesn't know of any work with that name.
error-mcp-shutting-down = ordin is closing, so that step wasn't started. Try again after it restarts.
error-mcp-socket-unavailable = ordin couldn't open the connection the assistant needs. Close other copies of ordin and try again.
error-mcp-tool-not-offered = That action isn't available for this work.
error-mcp-tool-spec-invalid = One of the actions offered to the assistant is set up incorrectly, so it can't be used.
error-mcp-too-many-calls = Too many steps are running at once. Wait a moment and try again.
